[2026-05-12T11:40:15.372Z] [INFO] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_520","type":"reasoning","text":"**Evaluating log management**\n\nI need to update my plan for a clean working tree since the ci-logs are currently untracked. The user mentioned that saving logs would help with reviews, but they also want the workspace to be clean. I’m wondering if it's acceptable to leave the untracked files or if I should remove them entirely. Maybe I can add ci-logs to .git/info/exclude to maintain a clean status while still preserving logs locally. But, hmm, that doesn't exactly fit what's requested!\n**Deciding on log exclusion**\n\nI'm considering whether to add `ci-logs/` to `.git/info/exclude` using shell commands, as modifying local git info is separate from the repository file. The developer suggested using apply_patch for manual edits. However, since the user wants to save the logs for easier review, I'm weighing the benefits of hiding them to maintain a clean status. I need to check if there are other untracked files too since the final build could have generated modifications that should also be evaluated."}}
